# PulseVault Meteor demo — environment variables.
#
# Meteor doesn't read `.env` automatically — export these in your shell before `meteor run`,
# or run `node --env-file=.env $(which meteor) run`. `.env` is gitignored; never commit secrets.

# Where uploads (and the demo's own feed/tickets file) are stored. Meteor bundles run from a
# generated build directory, not this source tree, so this must be an absolute path if you want
# uploads to persist across restarts — otherwise a tmpdir that's wiped on reboot.
PULSEVAULT_DIR=

# Signs the capability tokens in every pairing link. Required for anything but local play;
# the insecure built-in default only works on localhost.
PULSEVAULT_SECRET=

# The token issuer and the origin the phone uploads to. Meteor sets it from --port / your host.
# ROOT_URL=https://huddle.example.org
